{"title":"Mock AIME I 2012 Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Eli has 5 strings.  He begins by taking one end of one of the strings, and tying it to another end of a string (possibly the same string) chosen at random.  He continues on by tying two randomly selected untied ends together until there are no more untied ends, and only loops remain.  The expected value of the number of loops that he will have in the end can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/4/084079bf1d54500f3c59257a7ec3467932b72ba2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"34\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are relatively prime positive integers.  Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/3/0d3cbf9ab1e976e485e5a8b8459491ffa0b561dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> denote the expected value for the number of loops if there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> strings in the bag.  We proceed to condition on what happens with the first string.  There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f9a96c63183be91b9fe70e6e16dfa4bfec6f3da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> other string ends, 1 of which is on the same string.  If Eli ties the string to itself, then there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdca93962a2beaffc172ca394e04fe05bd74ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> remaining strings (identical to starting with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdca93962a2beaffc172ca394e04fe05bd74ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> strings, and 1 loop).  Otherwise, there are simply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdca93962a2beaffc172ca394e04fe05bd74ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> remaining strings, and 0 loops.   Since he chooses an end to tie at random, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/d/8edbde858aeecc2569a74fabd64e86e9118c501f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[E_n = \\frac{1}{2n-1} \\cdot \\left(1+E_{n-1}\\right)+\\frac{2n-2}{2n-1}\\cdot E_{n-1} = \\frac{1}{2n-1} + E_{n-1}.\\]\" width=\"474\" height=\"37\" />  Obviously, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/0/0103728ca271a685c660c37b569c8c73e0c03d7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E_1 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> (since the string will be tied to itself).  Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/a/beab87c942286b875ff47405e2fe0e0997e6fd42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E_2 = \\frac{1}{2\\cdot 2 - 1} + E_1 = \\frac{1}{3} + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"222\" height=\"37\" />; continuing on, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/3/4532e3395317966c718c850c6f4f4fc7ce8ebda6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E_n = \\sum_{k=1}^n \\frac{1}{2n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"129\" height=\"48\" />. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/c/cec8880cb0184b9cccf38ff0e1c61aaa2c7c3d7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E_5 = 1 + \\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{1}{7}+\\frac{1}{9}=\\frac{563}{315}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"249\" height=\"38\" />.  The desired answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/a/68aa141e3c36c20748f869675319b3fe6a4d00a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b=563+315=\\boxed{878}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"204\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"Mock AIME I 2012 Problems/Problem 7\"> Next Problem</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"Mock AIME I 2012 Problems/Problem 5\"> Previous Problem</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems\" title=\"Mock AIME I 2012 Problems\">Mock AIME I 2012 Problems</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018040819\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.012 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.023 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 88/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3038/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:10995:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018040819 and revision id 244735. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}